      "claim": "The commit turns an existing certifying test red. TestGoalBranchReadRealDelegateReachesSelectedClaude is the end-to-end test that drives `goal branch read --selected-installation` through the built engine to a fake claude. It passes on the parent and fails on this commit. The commit deletes the roster bridge (criticDelegateEnvironment) as the design directs, but it leaves this test unchanged. The test's goal worktree is not one Git maps to the selected installation, so the critic now gets the worktree's own roster model. The commit should rewrite the test's bed to a primary-serving worktree, or retire the test with a reason; shipping it red breaks the lane that certifies the unit.",
